# OptiX in the window, driven by scripted input (see docs/viewer.md, "Scripted input"), recorded and replayed. It quits
# by itself, at frame 72, so it runs without --exit-when-done:
#   RayTracingViewer sunlit -w 320 --height 180 --strata 4 -s 16 --input tests\window-optix.input --record r.txt
#                    --frames A --stats s.csv
#   RayTracingViewer --headless --script r.txt --record r2.txt --frames B
# Every frame in A equals the one in B of the same number (decoded), and r2.txt equals r.txt but for each frame line's
# gen: where a new session starts, a replay counts two generations (use_settings makes the session, and the frame
# line's new gen starts its image again) and the window one, as replays have always recorded. P's printed command, run,
# renders P's PNG and PFM, and s.csv has one "# model read" line per glTF file over all the Tabs (gpu_scene keeps the
# last two models: the bust and the vase are read once, by still-life). The keys come every few frames: the image
# needn't be done for them, as the recording holds each frame's passes and rows wherever the clock left them.
#
# O on sunlit: OptiX on, a new session at the same view (the first one compiles OptiX's programs, once per driver: the
# window says so and stands still meanwhile)
at 5 key O
# Tab: in a session with OptiX the scene after sunlit is still-life (the marble bust and the brass vase, read now)
at 10 key Tab
# A double-click on the bust (left of the image's middle, at the height of its chest): OptiX's pick finds the
# triangles, which the CPU's world doesn't hold, and the focus moves to them
at 20 mouse-down left 118 100
at 20 mouse-up left 118 100
at 20 mouse-down left 118 100 2
at 20 mouse-up left 118 100 2
# still-life's view saved as still-life-view-NNN.png and .pfm in the current folder, and its RayTracingGPU command
# printed (without --optix: a scene with triangle meshes implies it)
at 25 key P
# O on still-life: refused, as a scene with triangle meshes always traces with OptiX ("Note: still-life has triangle
# meshes: always OptiX", on the console and on screen); the session stays
at 28 key O
# Tab on through busts and cornell-bust, around to the books' first scene, materials, under OptiX (Tab keeps it), and
# Shift+Tab back to still-life: no model read again
at 30 key Tab
at 35 key Tab
at 40 key Tab
at 45 key-down Left Shift
at 45 key Tab
at 50 key Tab
at 55 key Tab
at 55 key-up Left Shift
# Shift+Tab once more: sunlit, the scene before still-life, at the view it opened with and still under OptiX (Tab keeps
# it; the Scene line names OptiX's programs)
at 60 key-down Left Shift
at 60 key Tab
at 60 key-up Left Shift
# F2 under OptiX: refused ("Note: OptiX computes in float32 only: O to turn it off first"); the session stays
at 63 key F2
# O: OptiX off, sunlit in a new session at the same view with the command line's kernel, auto, which for sunlit is the
# quality kernel (the Scene line names it; "OptiX off" on screen; kernel auto in the recording)
at 66 key O
# Tab without OptiX: the cycle without the scenes of glTF models, where the scene after sunlit is materials, under the
# books' kernel
at 69 key Tab
at 72 quit
